# Benchmark results and checkpoints
#
# The tree is ignored by default because a run leaves its persisted memory
# stores behind: 4.1 GB across 222,485 files for the ten LoCoMo conversations,
# which would exceed GitHub's limits and make clone times useless. They are also
# regenerable, and only worth keeping locally so retrieval-phase experiments can
# replay against them without re-ingesting.
#
# The per-question JSON for the two runs the README cites is the exception. It
# is ~10 MB, and without it every figure in the results section is a number a
# reader has to take on trust -- _summarise_locomo.py regenerates the whole table
# from these files. Re-including them requires un-ignoring the directory first;
# git cannot re-include a file whose parent directory is excluded.
scripts/benchmarks/results/**
!scripts/benchmarks/results/full_v2/
# Re-ignored as a directory, not a glob, so git prunes the subtree instead of
# walking 222k files on every status call. Un-ignoring full_v2/ above is what
# forces the descent; this stops it at the door.
scripts/benchmarks/results/full_v2/stores/
!scripts/benchmarks/results/full_v2/results.json
!scripts/benchmarks/results/full_v2/checkpoint_*.json
!scripts/benchmarks/results/full_v2.log
# Run logs (--log-file), hundreds of KB per run and reproducible from a rerun
logs/

# OS files
.DS_Store
generate_arch_diagram.py
DEMO_SCRIPT.md
NMAFC_Architecture.pdf